{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 4, :comments ["<b>I am weary with my calling out; my throat is parched.</b> — נחר is from the root חרה, like נחרתה; the nun is radical-less [weak/unstable], as in: אל מקדשי כי נחל. It is a niphal of a doubled-root [binyan nif'al of pe'alei ha-kafel]." "<b>My eyes fail.</b> — because he is hoping."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 69, :notes {0 "The citation 'אל מקדשי כי נחל' does not correspond to any known biblical verse; it may be corrupt or a paraphrase. Rendered hyper-literally."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:33:21.496655453Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}